---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { ATTRIBUTION } from '../../packages/contracts/trade';
import { href } from '../lib/data';
---

<Layout
  title="Sources and provenance"
  description="Official source references, statistical definitions, attribution, and the status of the sample preview."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">SHOW YOUR WORK</p>
    <h1>Sources you can inspect.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      This preview contains synthetic fixtures. Its figures were not retrieved
      from the Census Bureau. The official sources below define the planned live
      connector.
    </p>
    <h2>US Census Bureau — international trade</h2>
    <p>
      The live service is designed for monthly US merchandise trade: general
      imports at customs value, and total exports at free alongside ship (FAS)
      value. API credentials stay in the ingestion job.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="https://www.census.gov/data/developers/data-sets/international-trade.html">
          International Trade API documentation
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/imports/hs/variables.html">
          Import variables and metadata
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/exports/hs/variables.html">
          Export variables and metadata
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://www.census.gov/foreign-trade/guide/sec2.html">
          Statistical definitions
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://www.census.gov/data/developers/about/terms-of-service.html">
          API terms of service
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Attribution for the future live service</h2>
    <blockquote>{ATTRIBUTION}</blockquote>
    <p>
      No Census logo, seal or government imagery is used. Calculations and
      presentation are this project's work.
    </p>
    <h2>How publication will work</h2>
    <p>
      Acquisition, schema checks, coverage checks and reconciliation precede
      publication. Failed candidates remain unpublished. Each published page
      must identify its release and retain the corresponding dataset.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href={href('methodology/')}>Read the methodology →</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
